                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
&quot;at the same time as&quot; =&gt; is simultaneous with
&quot;together with&quot; =&gt; is simultaneous with
&quot;concurrently&quot; =&gt; is simultaneous with

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
&quot;during&quot; =&gt; is included in, NOT is simultaneous with
&quot;after&quot; =&gt; follows, NOT is simultaneous with
&quot;started with&quot; =&gt; begins, NOT is simultaneous with

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
&quot;The rash and the fever appeared together.&quot;
SOURCE: &quot;rash&quot; =&gt; finding; TARGET: &quot;fever&quot; =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is simultaneous with =&gt; TARGET
&quot;The chest pain and the dyspnoea began concurrently.&quot;
SOURCE: &quot;chest pain&quot; =&gt; finding; TARGET: &quot;dyspnoea&quot; =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is simultaneous with =&gt; TARGET
&quot;Fluids ran at the same time as the antibiotics.&quot;
SOURCE: &quot;fluid resuscitation&quot; =&gt; intervention; TARGET: &quot;antibiotics&quot; =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is simultaneous with =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that two findings or interventions occupy the same extent in time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType SIMULTANEOUS; interval semantics are time:intervalEquals, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000126</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is simultaneous with</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030">
        <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES: a clinical statement, MRI report, and discharge summary are information content entities.
NEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, pneumonia, and an MRI machine are respectively a clinical entity, finding, and physical object.
CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In &quot;The report states that the patient has pneumonia&quot;, the report is an information content entity; MRI report and discharge summary function similarly.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A generically dependent continuant that is about some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>information content entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


